On-device code model (Codes from messages > On this Mac)

Gemma is provided under and subject to the Gemma Terms of Use found at ai.google.dev/gemma/terms

The model that Bridgey by Round Robin downloads on first use (bridgey-otp-v<N>.gguf, from the
`models` release of github.com/round-robin-solutions/bridgey) is a Model Derivative of Gemma 3
270M (gemma-3-270m-it) by Google LLC. Round Robin modified it: the model was fine-tuned with LoRA
on synthetic text messages to find one-time codes, the adapter was merged into the weights, and
the result was converted and quantised to GGUF (Q4_K_M). It is not the original Gemma model and
is not endorsed by Google.

Use of the model is subject to the use restrictions in Section 3.2 of the Gemma Terms of Use,
including the Gemma Prohibited Use Policy (ai.google.dev/gemma/prohibited_use_policy). Bridgey's
model terms (licences/BRIDGEY-MODEL-TERMS.txt) make them a condition of using the model. Copies of
the Gemma Terms of Use and the Prohibited Use Policy are in licences/ and in the app under
Settings > About > Licences.

